    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 18 fields agree mathematically with their own captured worked solutions. q-71484: the gradient product rule gives e^{xy}(y(x²+y²)+2x, x(x²+y²)+2y). q-128529: fh=yz² on xyz≠0, so its gradient is (0,z²,2yz). q-110009: linearity gives 25(10)-10(3)+1=221. q-143820: the fourth moment is 0.25+6.4+4.05+38.4=49.1; the source's phrase 'each squared value' is an authored prose error, but its calculation correctly uses fourth powers. q-129892: the gradient is (2,-4), whose normalization is (1,-2)/√5, equivalent to the stated rationalized form. q-71374: the gradient is (-1,0), already a unit normal. q-71393 and q-130724: normal directions (-1,1) and (1,-1) give x+y=1 and x+y=2. q-65168 and q-37570: evaluating the gradients gives (3,-1,-1) and (4,1,4); q-65168 has an extra closing parenthesis in an intermediate source expression without affecting the result. q-37232: the normal direction is (4,1/2,-2), giving the stated symmetric line. q-37515: the gradient is (-1,-2,-1); reversing its direction gives the equivalent line x=(y+1)/2=z-1. q-181683: the shaded region lies between both solid lines, so (x,y)∈R² and -x-3≤y≤x+4. q-80643: equality of mixed partials gives 2a=3b, while -b+5=3 gives b=2 and a=3. q-65134: 2axy-3=4xy+b gives a=2 and b=-3. q-80753: pair I has unequal mixed partials, whereas II and III have equal mixed partials; III is considered on an open domain with y>0 and y≠1. No submitted-grade evidence was provided; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
